# The cases whose shape cannot exist on a platform, judged where it holds and
# skipped there by name with its reason (`.claude/rules/platforms.md`, the
# author's answer *A* of 2026-10-03, which says the same of a header a
# platform lacks; defect 640).
#
# **A skip here is a fact about C on that platform, never about the machine**:
# a missing header or library is `absence.hero`'s, asked of the machine each
# run. What stands here holds of every machine of the platform, so it is
# written down once with the measurement that found it, and a case or a
# surface row is named whole, so a renamed one stops being skipped and is
# judged, loudly, rather than skipped in silence (the test below holds each
# name to a case or a row that exists).
#
# **And a case whose words are one platform's is judged there alone**
# (defect 2053, 2026-10-13): clang refuses a header's `static` definition
# after the runtime's declaration on every platform, in other words on the
# Windows target than on this Mac and Linux, so each side's words are a case
# judged where they are said, and the refusal's mark, `#~`, on all three.
# **And a header's `static main` since defect 2253** (defect 2280,
# 2026-10-30): the runtime's `main` declared before any group's header, a
# header's `static` one follows it, and the Windows target tells it in the
# same extension's words, which the CI's Windows leg read first.

use <core>/strings as core_strings

use freed_bytes
use shell
use strings

# Why a case or a surface row named `name` is not judged on this machine, or
# absent where it is: on Windows, a shape its C cannot hold; anywhere else, a
# case whose words are the Windows target's alone; and off Darwin, a shape only
# Apple's clang reads (`darwin_alone`).
function reason(name: str) -> str?
    named: [Skip] @= elsewhere()

    if shell.exe_suffix() == ".exe"
        named @ windows()

    if !shell.exists(freed_bytes.DARWIN)
        named @ with_skips(list: named, more: darwin_alone())

    for one in named
        if one.name == name
            return ok(one.why)

    return fail(code: "judged", msg: "judged on this machine")

record Skip
    name: str
    why: str

constant INLINE_ON_WINDOWS: str
    "the Windows target reads C's `inline` as Microsoft's compiler does: a header's `inline` definition is emitted in every unit that calls it, a COMDAT the linker keeps once (clang -S -emit-llvm on the Windows box, 2026-10-11, clang 23.1.1), so a header-only C99 inline links there and the program prints 6, where C11 6.7.4p7 gives no external definition; it is judged on the platforms whose C reads the standard's rule (defect 640)"

constant STATIC_ON_WINDOWS: str
    "the Windows target reads a `static` definition after a function's external declaration as Microsoft's extension, which a header's region refuses in clang's words for it, `redeclaring non-static 'hero_str_len' as static is a Microsoft extension` (clang 23.1.1 on the Windows box, 2026-10-13), where this Mac's clang and Linux's say `static declaration of 'hero_str_len' follows non-static declaration`; no static shape is said alike on the three, so each platform's words are judged where they are said, these on this Mac and Linux, the `fixedbugs-2053-` cases on Windows, and every case's mark on all three (defect 2053)"

constant STATIC_ELSEWHERE: str
    "its words are the Windows target's, Microsoft's extension refused in a header's region (clang 23.1.1 on the Windows box, 2026-10-13), where this Mac's clang and Linux's say `static declaration of 'hero_str_len' follows non-static declaration`, which defect 2045's case judges on them; its mark is judged on every platform (defect 2053)"

constant STATIC_MAIN_ON_WINDOWS: str
    "the Windows target reads a header's `static int main` after the runtime's own declaration of `main` as Microsoft's extension, refused in a header's region in clang's words for it, `redeclaring non-static 'main' as static is a Microsoft extension [-Werror,-Wmicrosoft-redeclare-static]` (the CI's Windows x86-64 leg, run 41045262788, 2026-10-30), where this Mac's clang and Linux's say `static declaration of 'main' follows non-static declaration`; the runtime's `main` is declared before any group's header since defect 2253, and defect 2280's case judges the Windows words there"

constant STATIC_MAIN_ELSEWHERE: str
    "its words are the Windows target's, Microsoft's extension refused in a header's region (the CI's Windows x86-64 leg, run 41045262788, 2026-10-30), where this Mac's clang and Linux's say `static declaration of 'main' follows non-static declaration`, which `ffi-a-header-defining-a-static-main-is-told` judges on them; its mark is judged on every platform (defect 2280)"

constant LINKED_ON_WINDOWS: str
    "the probe of a header constant's value links on Windows with `/FORCE:UNRESOLVED`, the platform's word for leaving the program's libraries out, since neither link.exe nor lld drops a reference dead-stripping drops elsewhere (measured on the box, 2026-10-17); so a header constructor calling a function no library of the probe holds links there and ends the probe when it calls it, told as a probe that did not finish (measured on the box at bc978b09d: exception 3221225477 at the constructor's call), where Darwin's and Linux's links leave the symbol undefined and it is told by its name (panel 218's R2)"

constant CALLBACK_NAMED_ON_WINDOWS: str
    "Windows' stack guard says `stack exhausted` and names no function, the first sentence alone, so a case pinning the function a callback's frame ran out in is judged where a name is said, Darwin and Linux, and defect 2253's case on a spawned thread judges Windows (defect 2277)"

constant FRAME_NAMED_ON_WINDOWS: str
    "Windows' stack guard says `stack exhausted` and names no function, the first sentence alone, and its room's bound says it without a name too, so a case pinning which function's frame or room ran out at every level is judged where a name is said, Darwin and Linux, and defect 2253's cases judge Windows (defect 2339)"

constant INSTANCE_NAMED_ON_WINDOWS: str
    "Windows' stack guard says `stack exhausted` and names no function, the first sentence alone, and its room's bound says it without a name too, so a case pinning a generic function's instance by name, the frame or the room it ran out of, is judged where a name is said, Darwin and Linux, and defect 2253's cases judge Windows (defect 2371)"

constant LIBRARY_FILE_ON_WINDOWS: str
    "the Windows target links `-lh2476` as `h2476.lib` (`ffi_build.names_library`, measured on the box by panel 188 and beside defect 2398), a file of another name than the `libh2476.a` the case's folder holds for this Mac's ld64 and Linux's GNU ld, which read it under one name and refuse it in words read alike; so the file the expectation names cannot be the one the Windows link opens, and `link.exe`'s words for a file it cannot read are unrun (defect 2476)"

constant SECOND_EVENT_ON_WINDOWS: str
    "a second console event while the program stops is answered by Windows' own handler after the layer's, which ends the process with `STATUS_CONTROL_C_EXIT` (HandlerRoutine's page, read; the status unrun on the box), where POSIX's second SIGTERM ends it by the signal, 128 + 15 = 143, the status this case pins; no signal of POSIX's reaches a Windows program, so the shape is the stop's and the status the platform's, and the stop's other cases judge Windows' first event (panel 246's R4; lane b34-layer)"

# The cases and rows Windows cannot hold, by the name the report gives them.
function windows() -> [Skip]
    return [
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-562-a-header-only-inline-is-told-what-c-wants", why: INLINE_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "a header-only C99 inline is refused by run as by build, told what C wants (defect 562)", why: INLINE_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2045-a-header-that-defines-a-runtime-function-again-as-static-is-refused", why: STATIC_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2075-a-probe-that-does-not-link-is-told-as-such", why: LINKED_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "ffi-a-header-defining-a-static-main-is-told", why: STATIC_MAIN_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2277-a-callback-whose-frame-passes-the-stack-is-named-as-written", why: CALLBACK_NAMED_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2339-an-externs-large-result-aborts-in-the-function-that-called-it", why: FRAME_NAMED_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2339-an-externs-large-parameter-aborts-in-the-function-that-called-it", why: FRAME_NAMED_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2339-an-externs-large-parameter-and-result-abort-in-the-function-that-called-it", why: FRAME_NAMED_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2339-a-large-result-through-a-function-value-aborts-in-the-function-that-called-it", why: FRAME_NAMED_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2339-a-large-parameter-handed-on-to-an-extern-aborts-in-the-function-that-handed-it", why: FRAME_NAMED_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2339-an-externs-large-result-dropped-aborts-in-the-function-that-dropped-it", why: FRAME_NAMED_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2339-the-function-calling-the-extern-is-named-and-not-its-caller", why: FRAME_NAMED_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2339-a-generic-instance-calling-for-a-large-result-is-named", why: FRAME_NAMED_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2339-a-function-whose-room-is-full-is-named-at-every-level", why: FRAME_NAMED_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2371-a-generic-instance-that-recurses-for-ever-is-named", why: INSTANCE_NAMED_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2371-a-generic-instance-whose-room-is-full-is-named", why: INSTANCE_NAMED_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2476-a-file-the-linker-cannot-read-for-a-packages-library-is-told-at-its-package", why: LIBRARY_FILE_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2476-a-file-the-linker-cannot-read-for-a-link-is-told-at-the-group-that-links-it", why: LIBRARY_FILE_ON_WINDOWS)
        Skip(name: "the-platform-layer-ends-at-a-second-request-to-end", why: SECOND_EVENT_ON_WINDOWS)
    ]

# The cases whose words the Windows target's C alone says, by the name the
# report gives them, skipped on every other machine.
function elsewhere() -> [Skip]
    return [
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2053-a-header-that-defines-a-called-runtime-function-again-as-static-is-refused-on-windows", why: STATIC_ELSEWHERE)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2053-a-header-that-defines-an-uncalled-runtime-function-again-as-static-is-refused-on-windows", why: STATIC_ELSEWHERE)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2280-a-header-defining-a-static-main-is-told-on-windows", why: STATIC_MAIN_ELSEWHERE)
    ]

# `list` and then `more`.
function with_skips(list: [Skip], more: [Skip]) -> [Skip]
    out: [Skip] @= list

    for one in more
        out @ out.push(one)

    return out

constant EMPTY_CPATH_IS_APPLES: str
    "Apple clang 21 reads a `CPATH` set and empty as `.`, the folder clang runs in, and searches it before the platform's, where upstream clang adds nothing for an empty value (Debian clang 22.1.8's `clang -###`, panel 237's compiler-engineer, 2026-11-08): the shape is Darwin's, and its empty elements, `:` and a trailing separator, are judged everywhere (defect 2344)"

constant UNDERSCORE_STDIO_IS_DARWINS: str
    "Darwin's `stdio.h` includes `<_stdio.h>`, where glibc's and the UCRT's read no header of that name, so a program's own `_stdio.h` stands in for nothing there and the program builds; the shape is the SDK's (panel 237's compiler-engineer, 2026-11-08), and a library header the program's own header includes is judged everywhere (defect 2343)"

constant SOCKET_READS_TYPES_ON_DARWIN: str
    "Darwin's `sys/socket.h` includes `<sys/types.h>` itself, and the runtime's opening reads no `sys/types.h` there, so a program's own `sys/types.h` is read by the SDK's header after a header of the program's opened it, and the refusal names `<sys/socket.h>` as the includer (measured on this Mac, 2026-11-10, panel 243's critic and the lane b30-shadow); which header of glibc's or the UCRT's reaches `sys/types.h`, and whether the runtime's opening reads it first there, is unrun here, so these words are judged where they were read, and the rule that every include of a file is judged is held on every platform by `cli/shadowed_tree.hero`'s tests (defect 2447)"

constant TEXT_STUB_IS_APPLES: str
    "the folder `--library` names holds library `z` as a `.tbd`, a text stub Apple's linker reads as a library, so a tree that holds no binary carries a library of its own; GNU ld and lld-link read no `.tbd` and take the platform's `libz` beside it (measured on this Mac, 2026-11-11, at panel 245's landing; the other linkers' reading is their documented file types, unrun), so the shape, a library half a folder the build names holds, is judged on Darwin, and a header half the build names is judged everywhere (defect 2448)"

# The cases whose shape only Apple's clang or the SDK holds, skipped on every
# other machine by name, and two surface rows.
function darwin_alone() -> [Skip]
    return [
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2344-an-empty-cpath", why: EMPTY_CPATH_IS_APPLES)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2343-a-library-header-only-a-group-reaches", why: UNDERSCORE_STDIO_IS_DARWINS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2447-a-guarded-sibling-the-sdks-socket-header-includes-after-the-programs-header", why: SOCKET_READS_TYPES_ON_DARWIN)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2447-a-guarded-sibling-the-sdks-socket-header-includes-before-the-programs-header", why: SOCKET_READS_TYPES_ON_DARWIN)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2447-an-unguarded-sibling-the-sdks-socket-header-includes-after-the-programs-header", why: SOCKET_READS_TYPES_ON_DARWIN)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2447-an-unguarded-sibling-the-sdks-socket-header-includes-before-the-programs-header", why: SOCKET_READS_TYPES_ON_DARWIN)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2447-a-file-a-header-names-out-of-its-folder-the-sdks-socket-header-includes-after", why: SOCKET_READS_TYPES_ON_DARWIN)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2447-a-file-a-header-names-out-of-its-folder-the-sdks-socket-header-includes-before", why: SOCKET_READS_TYPES_ON_DARWIN)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2447-a-file-a-root-header-names-in-quotes-the-sdks-socket-header-includes-after", why: SOCKET_READS_TYPES_ON_DARWIN)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2447-a-file-a-root-header-names-in-quotes-the-sdks-socket-header-includes-before", why: SOCKET_READS_TYPES_ON_DARWIN)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2447-a-pragma-once-sibling-the-sdks-socket-header-includes-after-the-programs-header", why: SOCKET_READS_TYPES_ON_DARWIN)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs-2447-a-sibling-named-as-the-search-names-it-the-sdks-socket-header-includes-after", why: SOCKET_READS_TYPES_ON_DARWIN)
        Skip(name: "the platform's header beside a library of a folder --library names is refused as two releases (panel 245's R3, defect 2448)", why: TEXT_STUB_IS_APPLES)
        Skip(name: "a header and a library each of a folder the build names build, both halves named (panel 245's R3)", why: TEXT_STUB_IS_APPLES)
    ]

# **And an emission that names the platform's own C is compared where it was
# blessed** (defect 2111, 2026-10-17): since a group record's padding is zeroed
# before C reads it (panel 215's R1), a padding table and its macro guards name
# every member of the C struct as the machine's header declares it, private
# ones included, which no table may leave out, and those members are the
# platform's. The emission is right on each platform and one blessed file
# stands for all, so it is compared on Darwin, where this Mac blessed it, and
# skipped elsewhere by name; its program is built, run and emitted twice on
# every platform all the same (`run`, `warnings`, `determinism`).
constant MEMBERS_ARE_DARWINS: str
    "its emission names every member of a C struct as the machine's header declares it, a padding table and its macro guards (panel 215's R1): Darwin's `pthread_mutex_t` holds `__sig` and `__opaque` where glibc's holds `__align` and `__count`, Darwin's `regex_t` `re_magic`, `re_g` and `re_endp` where glibc's holds `__allocated`, and `struct addrinfo` puts `ai_canonname` before `ai_addr` on Darwin and after it on glibc (Linux arm64, Debian clang 22.1.8, 2026-10-17), and SDL3's `SDL_Event` holds `device_type` on this Mac where the CI's Linux x86-64 SDL3 holds `direction` there (defect 2113), and `struct passwd`'s `pw_change`, `pw_class` and `pw_expire`, Darwin's alone, in the table a record stored whole writes (defect 2112, found by lane `lane-s4` in Debian clang 22.1.8's emission), and `struct tm`'s `tm_gmtoff` and `tm_zone`, Darwin's and glibc's, which the UCRT's `struct tm` lacks (defect 2127, the CI's Windows leg, clang 20.1.8); blessed on Darwin and compared there, its program built, run and emitted twice on every platform (defect 2111)"

# **A padding table names no bit-field's byte since defect 2383**: C finds the
# bytes each named bit-field reaches before `main`, so a case whose table
# covers bit-fields is one text on every target and compared everywhere.
# `run/ffi-the-bits-beside-a-bit-field-are-zero` stood below from 2026-10-17
# (cec88be5e), its table naming `struct bf`'s bit-fields in bytes 1 and 2
# where the MSVC target puts them in 4 and 5.

# The emissions compared on Darwin alone, by the label `suite_emission` gives
# them.
function darwin_emissions() -> [Skip]
    return [
        Skip(name: "run/ffi-a-record-holding-a-lock-is-lent-in-place", why: MEMBERS_ARE_DARWINS)
        Skip(name: "run/lent-a-record-holding-a-lock-is-read-in-place", why: MEMBERS_ARE_DARWINS)
        Skip(name: "run/fixedbugs-094-the-systems-mutex-initialiser-builds-a-record", why: MEMBERS_ARE_DARWINS)
        Skip(name: "run/fixedbugs-173-a-regular-expression-gets-the-bytes-its-author-wrote", why: MEMBERS_ARE_DARWINS)
        Skip(name: "run/fixedbugs-a-tag-names-a-handle-and-a-record", why: MEMBERS_ARE_DARWINS)
        Skip(name: "run/ffi-a-construction-polls-an-sdl3-event", why: MEMBERS_ARE_DARWINS)
        Skip(name: "fixedbugs/a-header-field-that-is-not-const", why: MEMBERS_ARE_DARWINS)
        Skip(name: "examples/ctime/main", why: MEMBERS_ARE_DARWINS)
    ]

# Why the emission labelled `label` is not compared on this machine: one of
# `darwin_emissions` anywhere but Darwin, which a file every Darwin has tells
# (`freed_bytes.DARWIN`).
function emission_reason(label: str) -> str?
    if shell.exists(freed_bytes.DARWIN)
        return fail(code: "judged", msg: "judged on this machine")

    for one in darwin_emissions()
        if one.name == label
            return ok(one.why)

    return fail(code: "judged", msg: "judged on this machine")

# Whether the report a case's `!sanitizer:` line names is the runtime's to
# tell on this machine: a stack overflow on Windows, where ASan wrote nothing
# in 3 and 4 of 8 runs of one case and the runtime's handler keeps the fault
# (`runtime/parts/stack.c`, defect 641, measured on the Windows box
# 2026-10-11 with the CI's clang 20.1.8). Such a run is judged by the case's
# own ending, `!panic: stack exhausted`, as its `-O0` and `-O2` runs are.
function runtime_tells(needle: str) -> bool
    return shell.exe_suffix() == ".exe" && needle == STACK_OVERFLOW

constant STACK_OVERFLOW: str
    "stack-overflow"

## Tests

# Each name is a case of `tests/golden/` or a row the surface table names, so
# a case renamed or a row reworded is judged rather than skipped in silence.
test "every name skipped on Windows is a case or a surface row that exists"
    path = "tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-562-a-header-only-inline-is-told-what-c-wants.hero"
    assert shell.exists(path)
    assert windows()[0].name + ".hero" == "fixedbugs-562-a-header-only-inline-is-told-what-c-wants.hero"
    surface = read_file("tests/harness/suite_surface.hero")
    assert !surface.is_err()
    assert core_strings.contains(s: surface.must(), substr: "row(name: \"" + windows()[1].name + "\"")
    assert windows().len() == 20

    for one in windows().slice(from: 5, to: 17)
        assert shell.exists("tests/golden/run/" + one.name + ".hero")

    # Defect 2476's two folder cases, whose library file the Windows link
    # opens under another name.
    for one in windows().slice(from: 17, to: 19)
        assert shell.exists("tests/golden/unsupported/" + one.name + ".case/main.hero")

    # The stop's second request to end, whose end Windows' own handler
    # answers in a status of its own (panel 246's R4).
    assert shell.exists("tests/golden/run/" + windows()[19].name + ".hero")

    # Each case named for one platform's words is a case that exists, so a
    # renamed one is judged rather than skipped in silence (defect 2053).
    for one in [windows()[2], windows()[3], windows()[4], elsewhere()[0], elsewhere()[1], elsewhere()[2]]
        assert shell.exists("tests/golden/unsupported/" + one.name + ".hero")

    assert elsewhere().len() == 3

    # And each case judged on Darwin alone is a folder case that exists, or
    # a row the surface table names (panel 245's R3).
    for one in darwin_alone()
        folder = shell.exists("tests/golden/unsupported/" + one.name + ".case/main.hero")
        assert folder || core_strings.contains(s: surface.must(), substr: "row(name: \"" + one.name + "\"")

    # Two, defect 2447's ten danger cases, whose words are the SDK's, and
    # panel 245's two rows of a library a text stub holds.
    assert darwin_alone().len() == 14

# On a machine that is not Windows nothing is skipped by name but the cases
# whose words are Windows' alone, and on Windows those are judged.
test "a name is judged where its platform's C holds its shape"
    on_windows = shell.exe_suffix() == ".exe"
    assert reason("fixedbugs-562-a-header-only-inline-is-told-what-c-wants").is_err() == !on_windows
    assert reason("fixedbugs-2045-a-header-that-defines-a-runtime-function-again-as-static-is-refused").is_err() == !on_windows
    assert reason(elsewhere()[0].name).is_err() == on_windows
    assert reason("ffi-a-header-defining-a-static-main-is-told").is_err() == !on_windows
    assert reason("fixedbugs-2277-a-callback-whose-frame-passes-the-stack-is-named-as-written").is_err() == !on_windows
    assert reason("fixedbugs-2339-a-function-whose-room-is-full-is-named-at-every-level").is_err() == !on_windows
    assert reason("fixedbugs-2371-a-generic-instance-whose-room-is-full-is-named").is_err() == !on_windows
    assert reason(elsewhere()[2].name).is_err() == on_windows
    assert reason(darwin_alone()[0].name).is_err() == shell.exists(freed_bytes.DARWIN)
    assert reason("fixedbugs-562-another-case").is_err()

# Each emission compared on Darwin alone is a blessed file and a case that
# exist, `<group>/<stem>` as `suite_emission` labels it, so a renamed one is
# compared rather than skipped in silence; on Darwin every one is compared
# (defect 2111). A program of `examples/` is labelled by its path under the
# repository's root and a golden case by its path under `tests/golden/`, and
# the blessed file is the label with each `/` a `-` (defect 2127).
test "every emission compared on Darwin alone names a blessed file and a case that exist"
    for one in darwin_emissions()
        slash = strings.index_of(text: one.name, needle: "/")
        assert !slash.is_err()
        assert shell.exists("tests/emission/" + strings.split_text(text: one.name, separator: "/").join("-") + ".c")

        if one.name.slice(from: 0, to: slash.must()) == "examples"
            assert shell.exists(one.name + ".hero")
        else
            assert shell.exists("tests/golden/" + one.name + ".hero")

    assert darwin_emissions().len() == 8

    # No case is compared on Darwin alone for where a bit-field lies (defect
    # 2383): the emission of panel 223's case names no byte of one.
    for one in darwin_emissions()
        assert one.name != "run/ffi-the-bits-beside-a-bit-field-are-zero"

    on_darwin = shell.exists(freed_bytes.DARWIN)
    assert emission_reason(darwin_emissions()[0].name).is_err() == on_darwin
    assert emission_reason("run/another-case").is_err()

# A stack overflow's report is the runtime's on Windows alone, and no other
# report is (defect 641).
test "only a stack overflow's report is the runtime's, and only on Windows"
    on_windows = shell.exe_suffix() == ".exe"
    assert runtime_tells("stack-overflow") == on_windows
    assert !runtime_tells("on unknown address")
    assert !runtime_tells("heap-use-after-free")
